{"type":"standard","title":"Wolani language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Wolani language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q8029704","titles":{"canonical":"Wolani_language","normalized":"Wolani language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Wolani language</span></span>"},"pageid":34936705,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fa/Moanamani.jpg","width":200,"height":237},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fa/Moanamani.jpg","width":200,"height":237},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1265411630","tid":"8d1ae505-c3c8-11ef-9986-50194ce86ef3","timestamp":"2024-12-26T20:32:40Z","description":"Language in Central Papua","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolani_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolani_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolani_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Wolani_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolani_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Wolani_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolani_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Wolani_language"}},"extract":"Wolani (Wodani) is a Papuan language spoken by about 5,000 people in the Paniai lakes region of the Indonesian province of Central Papua. It is related to the Moni, Ekari, Auye, and Dao languages and may \nbe related to the Dani languages. Documentation is quite limited.","extract_html":"<p><b>Wolani</b> (Wodani) is a Papuan language spoken by about 5,000 people in the Paniai lakes region of the Indonesian province of Central Papua. It is related to the Moni, Ekari, Auye, and Dao languages and may \nbe related to the Dani languages. Documentation is quite limited.</p>"}